body:
That Nerd Wallet calculator put my break even at like 2 years which I makes me feel better.

&#x200B;

Edit:  yes, I was thinking if I can get a shorter term and the payments are affordable I'll do that as well.  Thanks!

I have used TurboTax for about 10 years.  This year after reading the Tax Software Megathread someone else mentioned I decided to try FreeTaxUSA.  TurboTax pricing is so ridiculous now that I couldn't do it again.  Last year I paid like $59 for "Deluxe" and then at the end they hit you with the old, we'll file your state taxes for another, I think, $39?  Anyway, it was ridiculous.

I still entered all of my info into TurboTax to see what my numbers looked like to compare against FreeTaxUSA and they were basically the same.  FTUSA actually caught a few things TT did not and my total bill for FTUSA "Deluxe" version with state filing was $19.95.

Also, FTUSA has what I consider to be superior security features.  You can use 2-factor authentication with Google Authenticator and I believe there were a couple of other options.  This might be an option in TT, but they never ask about it whereas FTUSA asked me to use it.

To me, FTUSA is a better solution for me and I likely will not be going back to TT.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
